                'content' => '<p>Three years ago I was charging $30/hr and constantly underbidding myself. Today I bill $150/hr with a waitlist. This isn\'t a flex — it\'s a roadmap, including the mistakes I hope you\'ll skip.</p><h2>Stop Selling Hours</h2><p>The first shift was psychological: I stopped selling time and started selling outcomes. Clients don\'t buy 40 hours; they buy a store that converts, a dashboard that loads instantly, a product that ships.</p><h2>Niche Down Hard</h2><p>Being a "full-stack generalist" means competing with everyone. When I specialized in e-commerce and SaaS dashboards, the same skills suddenly commanded premium rates from clients who needed exactly that.</p><h2>Results Over Effort</h2><p>I documented every project\'s before/after metrics. A portfolio of "I improved conversion by 40%" sells infinitely better than a portfolio of "I built this with React".</p><h2>Raise Prices on the Way Out</h2><p>Every raise was scarier than the last, and every raise lost a few clients — and those were exactly the clients I didn\'t want. The ones who stayed valued the work, not the discount.</p><p>Your rate is a signal. Raise it, and the market repositions you accordingly.</p>',
